content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-102, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-19870, filtered-water line (chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite)",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: 2.1 mm/s at the drive-end housing is in Zone A (0.0 to 2.8 mm/s RMS, 'New machines') of the HF-300 severity chart (Figure 3). It is well below the 4.5 mm/s Zone C 'plan maintenance' boundary and the 7.1 mm/s Zone D 'stop the pump' boundary. No vibration action is required. The manual says to classify the highest reading from both bearing housings, but only the drive-end reading was reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature: 66 C is within the documented normal range (normal up to 70 C; alarm 80 C; trip 90 C). Temperature is measured on the housing surface. No temperature action is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal leakage: a steady drip of about 1 drop per second. The evidence gives no numerical acceptable-leakage limit. The troubleshooting table treats 'leakage at shaft seal' as a fault whose corrective action is to replace the mechanical seal per 5.2 and check alignment per 5.4. The seal is therefore assessed as failed and due for planned replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Overall: vibration and temperature are normal, so there is no documented trigger to stop the pump immediately. The seal leak is a defect for planned replacement. Because the line is dosed with sodium hypochlorite, the leak should be contained and monitored until the work is done.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked seal faces. This is the most likely cause: the leak is isolated, with normal vibration and temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal run dry at some point, for example through loss of the Plan 11 flush from pump discharge. The manual states the seal must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. This is less likely given that drive-end vibration is in Zone A and temperature is normal, but the manual still calls for an alignment check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before isolation, record vibration on both bearing housings (drive end and non-drive end). Classify the highest reading using Figure 3, so there is a baseline and confirmation that the non-drive end is also in Zone A.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump. The pumped fluid is sodium hypochlorite-dosed water, so capture and contain drained fluid.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg) using lifting equipment. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the mechanical seal and shaft sleeve (HF3-455). Inspect the sleeve for scoring. Replace the sleeve if it is scored; the acceptance criterion for this serial is not documented (see open questions).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit a new component mechanical seal HF3-450 (correct for serial HF3-19870, which is below HF3-22000). Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120, which must be replaced whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten all fasteners to manual Table 5 (lightly oiled threads): seal gland nuts M10 to 25 Nm, impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm, casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm, bearing housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm. Do NOT use the 30 Nm gland torque from SB-2026-014; it applies only to HF3-450B on serial HF3-22000 and above.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool. This is required by the leakage corrective action and after work that moves the bearing housing. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is intact and the casing is filled. Never run the seal dry. After restart, check the seal for leakage. Re-measure vibration on both housings and confirm housing temperature is below 70 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Mechanical seal, component type (correct for serial HF3-19870, which is below HF3-22000)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Contingent: have one available, fit only if inspection shows scoring.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before any work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical hazard: the filtered-water line (P-101 to P-106) is dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Treat leakage and drained fluid as chemically contaminated, and contain and dispose of it accordingly.",
      "citations": [
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting: the back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, so lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the seal dry. Verify the Plan 11 flush and prime the pump before starting.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Stop criteria while waiting for repair: stop the pump if vibration on either housing reaches Zone D (7.1 mm/s RMS or above) or housing temperature reaches the 90 C trip. Raise the alarm at 80 C or on entry to Zone C (4.5 mm/s).",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h with 2 technicians (8.0 technician-hours).",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Estimated total: about 5.5 h elapsed and 9.5 technician-hours, excluding isolation and permits, which are not covered by the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number: the manual parts list specifies component seal HF3-450, while service bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes it with cartridge seal HF3-450B. The bulletin applies only to serial HF3-22000 and above. P-102 is serial HF3-19870, below that range, and the bulletin itself states that lower serials continue to use HF3-450. Decision: fit HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm, while SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. The 30 Nm value is limited to HF3-450B on serial HF3-22000 and above. Decision: for P-102 (HF3-19870), use 25 Nm per Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve replacement criterion: SB-2026-014 says to replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth, but only for serial HF3-22000 and above. The manual (5.2) says only to inspect the sleeve for scoring, with no limit. Decision: the 0.1 mm criterion does not formally apply to P-102; the limit is recorded as an open question.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "No acceptable seal leakage rate is documented. Can the pump keep running at about 1 drop per second until a planned window, and what leak rate should force an earlier shutdown?",
    "There is no sleeve scoring acceptance limit for pumps below serial HF3-22000. Should the 0.1 mm criterion from SB-2026-014 be adopted as engineering judgement, or is there a manual value?",
    "Non-drive-end vibration and temperature were not reported. The manual requires classifying the highest reading of both housings.",
    "Is the reported 2.1 mm/s an RMS velocity value, as Figure 3 assumes?",
    "Site-specific PPE, isolation and permit requirements for sodium hypochlorite-dosed fluid are not covered; only the dosing fact is given.",
    "Root cause history: has the seal flush (Plan 11) ever been lost, or has the pump run dry? This affects whether a repeat failure is likely.",
    "Stock availability of HF3-450, HF3-120 and HF3-455 is not confirmed.",
    "The required number of gland nuts and any O-rings or consumables for the seal change are not listed in the evidence."
  ]
}
